      "signpost": null,
      "definition": "used as the object of a verb or preposition to refer to the speaker or writer",
      "explanation": "**Me** is the object form; the subject form is **I**. In informal speech and writing, **me** is also common right after **be**: *It's me*; the more formal alternative, *it is I*, sounds stiff today.",
