  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "**Me** is not used as the subject of a sentence on its own; the subject form is **I**. When **me** is joined with another person as an object, either order is heard, but putting the speaker last is the more polite and widely taught order: *between you and me*, not *between I and you*.",
